{
  "doc": "M3-C06-02 greybox: ch06/brine_shoals (act1_ch06.md B01-B10). North is -z. From the south edge (Entry, the road from Pemakar's harbour) a line of wreck-ridges runs north: the Lit Age wreck (W01, banter 1), the midday hull (W02), the chalk-marked hull (W03, banter 3), then the last ridge and the hulk with the hold (W04, W08). West of the ridges lie the mud-flats, the slower short-cut. North of the last ridge is the Saltwright salvage camp (tents, lamp racks, the brazier, the burning hulk, the tide-wheel), and west of the camp the shoal channel, wide enough for the Warden's barge (W10-W13). East of the camp, the high hull where the party camps at dusk (W15: the fire, the Level-stone shrine in a wreck's bow, the vendor's boat), and below it the tideline (W16, B09). The channel runs out north (B10, to Tamsule). Everything is flat for the controller; ridges and the channel are painted slabs. Random fights (encounters) run only on the road, between ch06_arrived and ch06_sheltered_liss: the camp has none. states (Ch04Zone): the barge, Sefir and the Reeds hidden until the Inquisitor yields; Liss from her run; the raid's cast gone once she has joined; the party at the fire and Liss on the tideline at dusk. lights (Ch06Zone): the dusk after ch06_camp_made. Env-art's Brine Shoals kit (M3-ENV-02) dresses it: brine_shoals_dressing.json (tools/act1/ch06_brine_shoals_dressing.py, ZoneKitDressing, ADR 0200) hides the block meshes and keeps their collision; ChannelWater keeps Rhen out of the channel's water; the sun is the colour script's ch06 frame (35 deg, azimuth 240).",
